  i have a lot of work to do  i got to keep getting better my mindset  never going to change  but just being in that conversation in  the same centers with them that  that means a lot to me and it wouldn't  be possible without hard work so i just  gotta  focus what i do best which is you know  keep working hard  yeah you you talk about getting better  and i look at your career numbers  and in every season your points and  rebounds  have increased just from scoring from 7  to 13 to 17 to 23 to 27 to 28  to just under 30 this season so what is  it that you do  in between seasons in the off season  to improve your game  i tried to start the game try to spend  as much time as i can in the gym  trying to sharpen my tools just  know the game obviously as you grow  older you get more mature  you can play the game better but at the  end of the day you got to put as many  hours  as you can in to work in a jump shot to  work on your post moves to work on your  passive  uh and it's something i love to do i  always love to get in the gym  work hard for a summer two three months  and then in the season see the results  that of all the work i did  and i it's something that excites me  something that motivates me and  some that i always look forward to every  uh every summer  yes i did a series of interviews during  the hiatus before play began with a  number of  players around the nba and including  dirk nowitzki and it was interesting  when i talked to dirk about his mvp  season it had come in the same year that  his team had been knocked out of the  playoffs early and he said it was  it was kind of a strange feeling to get  the award and then still  feel the disappointment of of the  playoffs and i'm not saying that's the  way you have to feel but how do you  resolve those two feelings going on  right now with you  obviously i would love to be still in  the bubble keep playing games being the  second spanish you know fighting to uh  get opportunity to play in the finals  uh but